   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the city of Hudson to impose hotel and motel taxes, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7538",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7538-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 465 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7538\n\nSPONSOR: JORDAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the city of Hudson to impose hotel and motel\ntaxes, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would extend authorization for the City of Hudson to collect\nan occupancy tax on short-term lodgers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 extends Chapter 465 of the Laws of 2016, which authorizes the\nCity of Hudson to impose an occupancy tax for hotels and motels, until\n2025.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe tourism industry is a major part of the Hudson Valley's economy as a\nwhole. The lodging industry is an important component of the City of\nHudson's economy in particular. This legislation, introduced on behalf\nof the City of Hudson, would extend their authorization to impose an\noccupancy tax short-term, which it gained in 2016 and was extended in\n2019. This authorization is set to expire at the end of 2022, and this\nbill would extend it through 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSimilar to Ch. 567 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nThis will continue be beneficial to the City of Hudson and its resi-\ndents.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
